---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import WikiCard from '../components/WikiCard.astro';
import CategoryHub from '../components/v2/templates/CategoryHub.astro';
import { getPageSEO } from '../utils/seo';

const pageSEO = getPageSEO('recipes');
---

<BaseLayout pageId="recipes" breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: pageSEO.h1 }]}>
  <CategoryHub
    title={pageSEO.h1}
    kicker="Recipe hub"
    intro="Use the Recipe Hub to connect documented recipe information with ingredients, food, cooking, and serving guides."
    relatedLinks={[
      { label: 'Beginner Guide', href: '/guides/beginner-guide/', description: 'Learn how recipes fit into the complete restaurant service loop.' },
      { label: 'Cooking and Serving Guide', href: '/guides/cooking-and-serving/', description: 'Follow an order from the customer request through cooking and serving.' },
      { label: 'Ingredient Guide', href: '/ingredients/', description: 'Browse the ingredient directory and connected cooking information.' },
      { label: 'Equipment Guide', href: '/equipment/', description: 'Explore the restaurant tools used during food preparation.' },
    ]}
    relatedHeading="Related Guides"
    tableOfContents
  >
  <h2 id="introduction">Introduction</h2>
  <p>Recipes describe the relationship between a requested food item and its preparation information. In this Wiki, the Recipe Hub connects recipe-related questions with the separate sections for ingredients, food, grocery information, cooking, and serving.</p>
  <p>This hub brings those topics together without duplicating the individual category pages. Use the <a href="/food/">Food Directory</a> to browse the wider menu section, the <a href="/ingredients/">Ingredient Guide</a> for ingredient entries, and the <a href="/grocery/">Grocery</a> page for restocking information.</p>

  <h2 id="how-recipes-work">How Recipes Work</h2>
  <p>The Wiki organizes recipe information around this service relationship:</p>
  <p><strong>Order → Ingredients → Cooking → Food → Serving</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Order:</strong> identifies the requested food.</li>
    <li><strong>Ingredients:</strong> are the individual supplies documented in the ingredient directory.</li>
    <li><strong>Cooking:</strong> is covered by the task-focused cooking guide.</li>
    <li><strong>Food:</strong> is the category for prepared restaurant items.</li>
    <li><strong>Serving:</strong> connects the prepared item with customer service.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="featured-content">Featured Content</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <WikiCard title="Cooking and Serving Guide" description="Follow the complete restaurant workflow from reading an order to serving the customer." href="/guides/cooking-and-serving/" icon="C" />
    <WikiCard title="Ingredient Guide" description="Browse ingredient entries and learn where they connect with cooking information." href="/ingredients/" icon="I" />
    <WikiCard title="Food Directory" description="Explore food categories and the wider menu section of the Wiki." href="/food/" icon="F" />
  </div>

  <h2 id="recipe-directory">Recipe Information</h2>
  <p>The Wiki does not currently publish unverified individual recipe entries. Use these established sections to move between recipe questions and the systems connected to them.</p>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <WikiCard title="Food Directory" description="Browse the food category and its related Wiki content." href="/food/" icon="F" />
    <WikiCard title="Ingredient Directory" description="Open the directory of individual restaurant ingredients." href="/ingredients/" icon="I" />
    <WikiCard title="Grocery" description="Review ingredient sourcing and management information." href="/grocery/" icon="G" />
    <WikiCard title="Cooking Equipment" description="Browse the equipment topics currently covered by the Wiki." href="/equipment/" icon="E" />
  </div>

  <h2 id="cooking-and-order-flow">Cooking and Order Flow</h2>
  <p>Begin with the customer order and read the complete request before moving into food preparation. Use the ingredient and food sections when you need context for what is shown, then keep the order connected with the correct cooking task.</p>
  <p>Once the food is prepared, continue through the normal serving workflow and make sure it reaches the intended customer. When several restaurant tasks need attention, keep each order easy to identify from the request through service.</p>

  <h2 id="gameplay-tips">Gameplay Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Read the complete customer order before selecting ingredients or beginning preparation.</li>
    <li>Check the Ingredient Directory when an item in an order is unfamiliar.</li>
    <li>Keep the cooking area organized so active orders remain easy to follow.</li>
    <li>Match prepared food with the intended customer before completing service.</li>
    <li>Use the Food, Grocery, and Equipment sections for information outside the recipe directory.</li>
  </ul>
  </CategoryHub>
</BaseLayout>
